    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "City Centre residential dwelling/redevelopment opportunity."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "The property comprises a semi-detached two-storey residence which previously traded as a shop at ground floor level. The property has two large rooms at ground floor level with a hallway in between providing stairs to the first floor and a door to a side passageway which leads to the rear garden. The first floor has three bedrooms and a main bathroom. There is a mixture of window types throughout the property, with timber\r\nframe single glazed windows downstairs and newer PVC double glazed windows upstairs. The property requires modernisation.\r\n\r\nThe property has a very long rear garden and rear access. The passageway to the side of the property also has front access from Broad Street. The property will lend itself to residential use or possible conversion to multiple units and/or extension to the rear (subject to any necessary planning permission).\r\n\r\n(Please note the entire building is currently in use as residential - not commercial)\r\nTotal floor area – approx. 93.6 m² (1,007 ft²)\r\nGround floor - 49.07 m² (528 ft²)\r\nFirst floor - 44.53 m² (479 ft²)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "The property is situated in Broad Street in Limerick Centre.\r\nBroad Street connects John Street to Charlotte Quay and is within walking distance to the new Opera Centre, St. John’s\r\nHospital and Limerick School of Art and Design."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: G"
      },
      {
